  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Station Sign",
    "overview": "Marea treats a course as a metro line and every lesson as a station on it. The whole interface is lettered like mid-century enamel station signage: a warm grey ground, white enamel panels with a thin hairline, a near-black wall for the sidebar, and one line colour per course that does all the colour work. The chrome itself is colourless; colour arrives only from the line the learner is riding.\n\nDensity is calm and book-like. One centred column of panels, generous padding inside each, big Archivo titles over quiet Noto Sans reading text. Depth is flat: panels separate from the ground by tone and a 1px hairline, never by shadow. Motion is small and purposeful: the current station's ring grows in once, a pointed station swells a little, the segmented chip and the lesson stepper glide with a strong ease-out.\n\nThe signature is the line rail, drawn wherever progress shows: the home path, the ten-step lesson stepper. Done stations are filled, today's is a large ring, those ahead are hollow, revisions carry a second interchange ring.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One line colour per course, set each frame; it fills the primary button, the selected nav item, the band and the travelled rail.",
      "Archivo Bold and SemiBold for signage (titles, band, badges, station names); Noto Sans for everything read.",
      "Square-ish corners: 3px tiles, 4px controls, 6px panels.",
      "Flat enamel panels on a warm grey ground; a near-black station wall on the left.",
      "Drawn one-stroke icons, never emoji or typed symbols.",
      "Every colour has a light and a dark pair."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Line Rule",
        "body": "Colour on the chrome comes from the course's line colour and nothing else. A new surface takes `FILL`/`ACCENT` and their mixes; it never introduces its own accent hue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Dark Pair Rule",
        "body": "Every palette entry is declared as a light and a dark pair in `theme.rs`; marks drawn on the ground in a line colour go through `mark()` so they are lifted on dark.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Signage Voice Rule",
        "body": "Archivo is for things a station sign would say: titles, the band, badges, station names. Anything the learner reads at length is Noto Sans.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence Case Rule",
        "body": "Labels are sentence case at 13px medium muted. No uppercase tracking.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Enamel Flat Rule",
        "body": "Nothing on the page casts a shadow. Only floating layers (windows, popups, toasts) do.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do take every accent from the course's line colour (`FILL`, `ACCENT`, `ACCENT_SOFT`, `HOVER`) and put text on it with `text_on`.",
      "Do declare any new colour as a light and dark pair in `theme.rs`.",
      "Do set titles and signage in Archivo (`display`, `sign_family`) and reading text in Noto Sans.",
      "Do use the `Btn` variants (primary, secondary, ghost, on-line) so every button answers hover and press.",
      "Do draw progress as the line rail: filled done, ringed today, hollow ahead, double-ringed revisions.",
      "Do keep corners at 3px, 4px or 6px and panels flat with a 1px hairline.",
      "Do ease marks in with the shared cubic ease-out (`ease`, `glide`) at 0.12–0.24s."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't give the chrome its own accent hue or use the brand red outside the logo.",
      "Don't colour level badges per level; they are ink squares on one line.",
      "Don't put shadows under panels on the page.",
      "Don't use emoji or typed symbols as icons; draw them with `Icon`.",
      "Don't set uppercase tracked labels; labels are sentence case.",
      "Don't use Archivo for paragraphs, translations or notes."
    ]
  }
}